{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794336503","published":"2026-11-10T18:48:36Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:17:13.422001015Z","upstream":["CVE-2025-40778","CVE-2025-8677","CVE-2026-11622"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2025-40778, CVE-2025-8677, CVE-2026-11622","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: cache poisoning via too-lenient acceptance of\n     records into the resolver cache\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-40778.patch: only cache authority-section\n       NS RRsets that own an ancestor of the queried name and came over\n       TCP or were signed, use the NS owner name as the bailiwick apex\n       for cached glue, and retry responses with an unsigned DNAME over\n       TCP in lib/dns/resolver.c; add dns_message_hasdname() in\n       lib/dns/message.c\n     - CVE-2025-40778\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: CPU exhaustion via malformed DNSKEY records\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-8677.patch: fail the validation when a\n       DNSKEY matching the RRSIG or DS cannot be loaded instead of\n       trying the remaining keys in get_dst_key(), get_key() and\n       checkkey(), and no longer load and verify matching keys inline in\n       isselfsigned() in lib/dns/validator.c\n     - CVE-2025-8677\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: cache memory exhaustion by expired entries that are\n     not reclaimed while their node stays referenced\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-11622.patch: reference count the cache\n       rdataset headers and reap stale ones from the node's down chain as\n       soon as they are unreferenced; keep the header alive for the\n       noqname/closest proof rdatasets, which get their own slab_methods,\n       in lib/dns/rbtdb.c; bump MAPAPI to 1.2 since the header layout of\n       map-format files changes\n     - CVE-2026-11622","affected":[{"package":{"name":"bind9","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/bind9?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:9.10.3.dfsg.P4-8ubuntu1.19+tuxcare.els15"}]}],"dat